$NetBSD$

Origin: EmberBSD (AI-assisted), actual software GBM node selection.
Mesa KMS software rendering needs primary-node CREATE_DUMB and MAP_DUMB.
Retry only after EGL identifies its software device, retaining the caller's
primary authorization. Render-only callers fail; hardware paths are unchanged.
Keep caller, renderer and allocator GEM tables separate through the existing
reopen/lease/auth path. Clean up partially initialized private EGL displays.
No kernel permission changes or environment-based driver guesses.
Not submitted upstream.

